Step 8: Aptitude, reasoning and communication (from month 7)

Many campus drives start with an online aptitude test, and good coders get rejected here simply because
they never practised. Spend 30 minutes a day on it in the last four to five months.

Placement Roadmap for MCA Students 9
• Topics: percentages, profit and loss, time and work, speed and distance, ratios, probability,
permutations, number series, coding and decoding, blood relations, seating arrangements, reading
comprehension, grammar.
• Practise: IndiaBix (indiabix.com) and PrepInsta (prepinsta.com), which also has company specific
previous patterns.
• Communication: explain one concept out loud every day for two minutes, in English, as if teaching a
junior. Record it on your phone and listen once. It feels awkward, and it works.
